Kind Interface Built-ins (registry name) store <code>MemoryStore</code>: <code>insert</code>, <code>update</code>, <code>get</code>, <code>delete</code>, <code>query</code> (+ optional <code>vector_search</code>) <code>memory</code>, <code>sqlite</code>, <code>pgvector</code>, <code>qdrant</code> embedder <code>Embedder</code>: <code>embed(texts)</code> <code>hashing</code> (offline), <code>ollama</code> (local model), <code>openai</code>, <code>azure_openai</code>, <code>function</code>, <code>agno</code> extractor <code>Extractor</code>: <code>extract(messages, existing)</code> <code>rules</code> (offline), <code>llm</code>, <code>none</code> ranker <code>Ranker</code>: <code>rank(query, query_embedding, records, limit=, at=)</code> <code>hybrid</code> processor <code>Processor</code>: <code>process(candidate)</code> returns the candidate or <code>None</code> to drop it. A plain function works too. <code>drop_secrets</code> (default), <code>redact_pii</code>, <code>min_importance</code> summarizer <code>Summarizer</code>: <code>summarize(messages, previous)</code> <code>extractive</code>, <code>llm</code> adapter <code>Adapter</code>: <code>matches(target)</code>, <code>attach(target, memory, **options)</code>, optional <code>detach(target)</code> <code>agno</code>, <code>method</code>, <code>callable</code> intelligence <code>manage(memory, messages, ...)</code> - or replace one part: a router <code>route(memory, turn)</code>, a planner <code>plan(memory, query, ...)</code>, a scheduler <code>after_turn(memory, report, ...)</code> <code>heuristic</code>, <code>llm</code> <pre><code>from kioko import Adapter, Embedder, MemoryLayer, MemoryMiddleware, register

@register("embedder", "minilm")
class MiniLM(Embedder):
    def __init__(self):
        from sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer
        self.model = SentenceTransformer("all-MiniLM-L6-v2")
    def embed(self, texts):
        return self.model.encode(list(texts)).tolist()

@register("adapter", "my-framework")              # tried before the built-in adapters
class MyFrameworkAdapter(Adapter):
    def matches(self, target):
        return type(target).__module__.startswith("my_framework")
    def attach(self, target, memory, **options):
        hooks = MemoryMiddleware(memory, **options)
        target.before_turn(lambda t: t.add_context(str(hooks.before(t.text, user_id=t.user))))
        target.after_turn(lambda t: hooks.after(t.text, t.reply, user_id=t.user))
        return target

memory = MemoryLayer.from_config({          # or a path to a JSON file
    "store": {"type": "sqlite", "path": "memory.db"},
    "embedder": "minilm",                     # or {"type": "azure_openai", "deployment": "text-embedding-3-small"}
    "extractor": {"type": "llm", "llm": {"$import": "my_app.llm:complete"}},
    "processors": ["drop_secrets", "redact_pii"],
    "dedup_threshold": 0.92,
})
</code></pre> <p>Ship components in their own package so <code>pip install</code> is all it takes. <code>kioko components</code> lists everything that's available:</p> <pre><code>[project.entry-points."kioko.embedders"]
minilm = "my_plugin.embedders:MiniLM"

[project.entry-points."kioko.adapters"]
my-framework = "my_plugin.adapter:MyFrameworkAdapter"
</code></pre> <p>A custom store only needs five methods. See <code>examples/04_custom_components.py</code> for a JSON-file store in about 30 lines, and stores for the reusable contract tests. For a vector database (Azure AI Search, Elasticsearch, Milvus ...), implement <code>vector_search</code>, as the pgvector and Qdrant stores do. The extraction rules can be extended without a new extractor: <code>RuleBasedExtractor(extra_rules=[Rule("ticket", r"^my ticket is (?P&lt;id&gt;[A-Z]+-\d+)$", template="User's open ticket is {id}", key="work.ticket", flags=0)])</code>.</p>
